CLI tools 

    .program to be executed through a terminal using text commands 
    .accepts arguments, flags, and subcommands
        .performs operations
            .returns structured output 

    .foundational in: 
        .backend engineering
        .DevOps
        .automation
        .cloud infrastructure
        .data engineering
        .system administration

    .preferred because they are:
            .scriptable
            .fast
            .deterministic
            .remote-friendly
            .easy to integrate into pipelines

    
    Need for them:
        .automation - deployments/ migrations/ backups/ API interactions/ data processing/ environment setup
        .reproducibility - repeatable recipe - doing the same thing, on any machine
        .integration - with CI/CD pipelines, cron jobs, shell scripts, Docker containers, remote servers 
        .speed - eliminates UI overhead: perform complex task very fast
        .precision - no ambiguity/ no clicking the wrong button/ no UI bugs



    Composition
    .entry point 
        .the executable command
    .subcommands 
    .arguments 
        .values passed to commands
    .flags 
        .optional modifiers 
    .output 
        .human-readable or machine-readable (JSON)



How they are built:
    .Python 
        .using libraries like click, argparse, or typer 
    .Node.js 
        .commander/yargs
    .go
        .cobra - industry standard for cloud tools 
    .rust 
        .clap - high performance, safe 
    .shell 
        .bash scripts/ powershell scripts 




Need for building CLI tool for development:
    .controlling API from the terminal 
    .automating development workflow 
    .managing my database 
    .deploying my project
    .building a professional engineering toolkit 

    